You are a senior backend engineer, data engineer, AI systems engineer, and software architect.

I want you to BUILD the complete project described below from scratch.

PROJECT NAME:
Closed-Loop Autonomous Data Incident Agent

PROJECT GOAL:
Build a production-style autonomous data incident resolution platform that can detect data incidents, investigate their root cause, propose a remediation, safely simulate the remediation, verify the result, calculate risk, either automatically deploy or request human approval, verify the production result, rollback if necessary, and store the incident/fix outcome as memory for future incidents.

This should NOT be a simple chatbot.

It should be a real software system where:
- deterministic software handles safety-critical operations
- AI agents handle investigation/reasoning
- agents NEVER get unrestricted production access
- every proposed action passes through a control/policy layer
- fixes are tested in a sandbox before production
- verification is mandatory
- risky operations require human approval
- successful incidents are stored in vector memory
- similar future incidents can reuse previous solutions

The final project should be portfolio/resume quality and demonstrate:
- Backend engineering
- Data engineering
- SQL
- Python
- FastAPI
- PostgreSQL
- Exasol
- LangGraph
- LLM agents
- Qdrant
- data quality
- observability
- workflow orchestration
- sandbox execution
- risk management
- human-in-the-loop systems
- rollback
- auditability
- Docker
- testing
- clean architecture

==================================================
1. HIGH-LEVEL SYSTEM
==================================================

Implement this closed loop:

DETECT
   ↓
INVESTIGATE
   ↓
ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS
   ↓
GENERATE REMEDIATION
   ↓
POLICY / CONTROL CHECK
   ↓
SIMULATE IN SANDBOX
   ↓
VERIFY
   ↓
RISK ASSESSMENT
   ↓
AUTO DEPLOY OR HUMAN APPROVAL
   ↓
PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT
   ↓
POST-DEPLOY VERIFICATION
   ↓
PASS → CLOSE INCIDENT
FAIL → ROLLBACK
   ↓
STORE INCIDENT + FIX + OUTCOME IN MEMORY
   ↓
LEARN FROM PREVIOUS INCIDENTS

The system should behave like an autonomous data reliability engineer.

