POST /incidents/{incident_id}/deploy

POST /incidents/{incident_id}/rollback

GET /incidents/{incident_id}/timeline

GET /incidents/{incident_id}/risk

GET /incidents/{incident_id}/lineage

GET /incidents/{incident_id}/simulation

GET /health

Also provide an endpoint to trigger failure scenarios, for example:

POST /scenarios/{scenario_id}/inject

This should allow testing.

==================================================
25. FAILURE INJECTION SYSTEM
==================================================

Create a deterministic failure injection framework.

Example:

POST /scenarios/SCN-02/inject

It should:
- create the failure
- create/update relevant metadata/logs
- trigger detection
- create incident
- start workflow

Also provide:

POST /scenarios/reset

This should restore the clean baseline.

The user must be able to repeatedly run:

RESET
→ INJECT FAILURE
→ DETECT
→ INVESTIGATE
→ FIX
→ SIMULATE
→ VERIFY
→ DEPLOY
→ VERIFY
→ CLOSE

==================================================
26. FIRST DEMO SCENARIO
==================================================

The primary demo must be SCN-02 Schema Change.

Expected demo:

1. System is healthy.
2. Inject schema change.
3. Pipeline fails.
4. Observability detects incident.
5. FastAPI receives incident.
6. LangGraph starts.
7. Investigator:
   - checks pipeline logs
   - checks schema history
   - checks lineage
   - queries Exasol
   - searches Qdrant
8. Investigator identifies root cause:
   source column changed from customer_id to customer_identifier.
9. Engineer generates transformation mapping fix.
10. Control layer validates SQL.
11. Sandbox executes fix.
12. Verifier confirms:
   - rows restored
   - NULLs fixed
   - downstream metrics correct
13. Risk engine evaluates.
14. If safe, auto-deploy.
15. Production verification passes.
16. Incident closes.
17. Full incident/fix/outcome stored in Qdrant.

This should be the "hero demo" of the project.

==================================================
27. SECOND DEMO SCENARIO
==================================================

Also fully support NULL Explosion.

Example flow:

1. Inject NULL corruption.
2. Detection engine detects abnormal NULL rate.
3. Investigator checks historical quality metrics.
4. Investigator checks pipeline logs.
5. Investigator checks transformation.
6. Root cause identified.
7. Engineer proposes fix.
8. Sandbox.
9. Verification.
10. Risk.
11. Deployment/approval.
12. Production verification.
13. Memory storage.

